# Integrity pin for the trusted-firmware source scripts/build-agsim.sh compiles and
# runs. The source comes from git, not the Go module proxy: the repository root
# has no go.mod, so proxy.golang.org and sum.golang.org serve no version of
# github.com/jeremyhahn/trusted-firmware, and go.sum cannot cover it. This file
# pins the commit and its tree instead.
# Format: <repository URL> <version> <commit sha> <tree sha>. Bumping the
# trusted-firmware/sdk/go dependency means adding the new version's line here,
# read from the repository, not from the tag name alone:
#   git ls-remote <URL> 'refs/tags/<version>^{}'                 (the commit)
#   git init t && git -C t fetch --depth 1 <URL> <commit> &&
#   git -C t rev-parse 'FETCH_HEAD^{commit}' 'FETCH_HEAD^{tree}'  (commit, tree)
https://github.com/jeremyhahn/trusted-firmware v0.4.2-alpha e0ae83d062b45dccc0e4cf08c87bf6def80a946c de53b2be47bdfdf05cc04432fdd997cf685794eb
